   {
    "t": 9.031,
    "type": "done",
    "data": {
     "answer": "Hybrid search without reranking lost to BM25 alone because the weaker vector ranking diluted good keyword results. Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) weights both rankers equally, so the vector results pulled down rankings that BM25 had already gotten right (0010-hybrid-retrieval-with-reranking.md, section \"Alternatives considered\").\n\nKeyword search alone matched reranked hybrid on hit@4 and cost almost nothing, but it ranked the right passage lower (MRR 0.85). The record notes that it would fail on paraphrased questions that share no words with the text, but this test set had few of those. That is why the project kept hybrid retrieval and added a reranker: the reranker corrects the ordering after fusion, which plain fusion did not do.",
     "sources": [
      "0010-hybrid-retrieval-with-reranking.md, section \"Alternatives considered\""
     ],
     "guard": "ok"
    }
   }
