    "data": {
     "answer": "The project chose Langfuse over LangSmith mainly for licensing and self-hosting reasons. Both tools offer similar features, but LangSmith is closed source and cannot be self-hosted on a free plan. Langfuse is open source (MIT), so it can be self-hosted later through the same API, and its cloud free tier is enough for this project. (0012-evaluation-harness-with-langfuse.md, section \"Alternatives considered\")\n\nThe record also notes that LangSmith is the native LangChain/LangGraph option with the same features, so the choice was not about missing functionality. The decision keeps the option open: the project can start on Langfuse Cloud and move to self-hosting later without changing the code.",
